  tcn="An exact algebraic (Pythagorean) identity -- the cross term vanishes because sum_j (X_ij - Xbar_i.) = 0 within each group. Under N(mu_i, sigma^2) errors and H0: all mu_i equal, Cochran makes SS_between/sigma^2 ~ chi^2_{k-1} independent of SS_within/sigma^2 ~ chi^2_{N-k}, so the F-ratio [SS_between/(k-1)] / [SS_within/(N-k)] ~ F_{k-1, N-k}.",
